From: baseband lane
Subject: 0512 pandora_pas: the metadata blob must live below 4 GiB

The 2026-11-21 probe sent the same DTB metadata blob for nine PAS ids -- including pas 0, which
cannot exist -- and TrustZone answered 0xffcfffbb (-3145797, invalid parameter) every single time.
So the rejection is about the buffer, not the id.

The blob the failing run used sat at 0x8d19a6000, above 4 GiB, while every address this platform
hands TrustZone for PIL is below it: modem carveout 0x8aa00000, DTB region 0x99500000, IPA firmware
0x99590000.  kmem_alloc_contig's min_addr/max_addr were both 0, i.e. no constraint at all.  They are
now 0 .. 0x100000000.

Note: the first hardware run of this call (the same log) also shows the full inputs now printed --
`pas 38 init_image (4044 bytes, arginfo 0x82, blob 0x8d19a6000)` -- so the next log says whether the
blob moved.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index e55b7d9..147c20b
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
@@ -178,8 +178,18 @@ pandora_pas_load(const char *prefix, const char *base, unsigned pas, uint64_t me
 	 * unmap panic was found first (patch 0507), and the kmem_free one line later would have
 	 * been the next boot's failure.
 	 */
-	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, 0, 0,
-	    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+	/*
+	 * Below 4 GiB on purpose.
+	 *
+	 * The 2026-11-21 probe sent the same metadata blob for nine different PAS ids and TrustZone
+	 * answered 0xffcfffbb (-3145797, "invalid parameter") every time -- including for pas 0, an
+	 * id that cannot exist -- so the rejection is about the buffer, not the id.  The blob the
+	 * first run used sat at 0x8d19a6000, above 4 GiB, while every address this platform hands
+	 * TrustZone for PIL (carveout 0x8aa00000, DTB 0x99500000, IPA 0x99590000) is below it.
+	 * kmem_alloc_contig's min_addr/max_addr were both 0, i.e. no constraint at all; give it one.
+	 */
+	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, 0,
+	    0x100000000ull, KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
 		err = ENOMEM;
 		goto out;
 	}
@@ -348,8 +358,18 @@ pandora_pas_init_only(const char *prefix, const char *base, unsigned pas, uint64
 	uint32_t hash_size = ph[hash].p_filesz;
 	uint64_t md_size = ((uint64_t)ehdr_size + hash_size + 0xfff) & ~0xfffull;
 	vm_offset_t md = 0;
-	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, 0, 0,
-	    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+	/*
+	 * Below 4 GiB on purpose.
+	 *
+	 * The 2026-11-21 probe sent the same metadata blob for nine different PAS ids and TrustZone
+	 * answered 0xffcfffbb (-3145797, "invalid parameter") every time -- including for pas 0, an
+	 * id that cannot exist -- so the rejection is about the buffer, not the id.  The blob the
+	 * first run used sat at 0x8d19a6000, above 4 GiB, while every address this platform hands
+	 * TrustZone for PIL (carveout 0x8aa00000, DTB 0x99500000, IPA 0x99590000) is below it.
+	 * kmem_alloc_contig's min_addr/max_addr were both 0, i.e. no constraint at all; give it one.
+	 */
+	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, 0,
+	    0x100000000ull, KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
 		err = ENOMEM;
 		goto out;
 	}
